Louis used invoice factoring, or accounts receivable factoring. Each week he presented invoices; the factoring company advanced cash against them. He describes the advance as around 90 percent of invoice value and the all-in cost as about 21 percent: $\begin{aligned}
A_{\mathrm{cash}} &\approx 0.90I,\\
i_{\mathrm{factoring}} &\approx 21\%.\end{aligned}$ Here $I$ is the invoice face value, $A_{\mathrm{cash}}$ is the cash advance, and $i_{\mathrm{factoring}}$ is the spoken all-in financing cost.

