p.src:
A weak theory of delegation says, assign tasks. Louis gives a stronger theory: $\text{real accountability}
\quad\Rightarrow\quad
\text{real authority}.$ If a person is responsible for outcomes but has no authority to act, accountability becomes punishment. Louis’s version gives people room to make decisions, take risks, and push the business beyond what the founder alone would see.

