The chapter’s sequence is: $\text{proof}
\rightarrow
\text{cash-flow discipline}
\rightarrow
\text{stronger balance sheet}
\rightarrow
\text{better capital}
\rightarrow
\text{larger contracts}
\rightarrow
\text{delegated scale}.$ The numbers are approximate interview claims, and they should remain source-conscious. But they carry a coherent commercial lesson: wealth here is not presented as one sudden breakthrough. It is a chain of constraints survived in the right order.

